+# Design
+
+## Approach
+
+Make category deletion operate on the complete descendant set, detach those category entities from each affected product, and never call product deletion. Persist the product updates before deleting categories so products with no remaining categories are still valid records. Keep cart and order entities untouched.
+
+The facade must resolve the category using the merchant store and throw the existing resource-not-found exception when absent. Product listing by category must naturally return an empty result for an absent category, while category reads use the same not-found behavior. The delete operation should remain store-scoped and transactional through the existing service transaction boundary.
+
+## Affected Areas
+
+- `CategoryServiceImpl.delete`: replace product deletion with association removal for the category tree.
+- Category facade/API lookup and deletion paths: consistently distinguish missing categories with 404.
+- Product/category query behavior: ensure absent category ids do not resolve stale products.
+- Core and API regression tests covering products, descendants, carts, orders, and 404 responses.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+No product, cart, or order schema changes are required. Existing products retain their identifiers and all non-deleted data, so downstream references remain valid.
