@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a category currently deletes products that have no remaining category, breaking inventory, carts, and orders. It can also leave category lookups inconsistent instead of returning the required not-found response.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Delete only the requested category and all descendants.
+- Remove deleted categories from product/category associations while preserving every product and its inventory, price, and other category associations.
+- Preserve cart and order references to affected products.
+- Return HTTP 404 for missing or deleted categories and ensure deleted-category product listings are empty.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `category-deletion`: Safe deletion of category trees without deleting products or invalidating product references.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The category service/facade and product-category persistence path are affected, along with category and product APIs and regression tests. Shopping-cart and order behavior must remain compatible because product records are retained.
